Backport of upstream pygfx PR #1315 (merged after the v0.17.0 release):
"Fix dashing on line loops and restart dashes per line piece"

    https://github.com/pygfx/pygfx/pull/1315
    https://github.com/pygfx/pygfx/commit/8c21370fc508e5b1223c58ecb54615b4c8e8f330

Fixes pygfx#1103: the segment that closes a line loop was measured with the
whole loop's length instead of its own, so its dashes came out
loop_length/segment_length times too dense (a dashed square rendered as a
solid line).  Dash phase is now also restarted at each line piece.

The upstream commit also adds tests and a validation example; those live
outside the sdist, so only the pygfx/ hunks are backported here.

